+# Deep OpenCode plugin integration for Forge
+
+- **Feature**: `opencode-plugin`
+- **Date**: 2026-09-11
+- **Status**: planned (Phase 2 research complete; review loop applied; task list drafted)
+- **Epic**: `06373ce8-d63e-4b04-9612-9b3c0486c4d5`
+- **Worktree**: `.worktrees/opencode-plugin` (branch `feat/opencode-plugin`, based on origin/master)
+- **Target**: opencode **v2 beta** only — `@opencode/cli@0.0.0-beta-19425` + `@opencode/plugin@0.0.0-beta-19425` (binary `opencode2`)
+
+## Purpose
+
+Forge currently reaches opencode only by accident: opencode discovers the committed
+`.agents/skills` mirror and `AGENTS.md`, but Forge dropped opencode as a supported harness in
+commit `71459355` (#204, decision `PD-20260611-supported-harness-set`). opencode v2 beta exposes
+a first-class plugin API (tools, commands, skills, sessions, permissions, events, storage, shell,
+MCP, TUI) that is richer than anything Forge integrates with today. This feature makes opencode a
+**first-class Forge surface** again via a native plugin: gates that actually bite at the moment of
+action, native Forge tools/commands/skills, and session orientation — while keeping the kernel as
+the single source of truth and the plugin read-only by default.
+
+## Approach selected
+
+**Vendored, zero-runtime-dependency plugin directory, delivered by `forge setup`.**
+
+A single self-contained `plugin/opencode/index.ts` (plain `export default { id, setup }` — no
+`import` statements; uses only the `Bun.spawn` global, verified available in the opencode2 plugin
+runtime) that shells out to the `forge` CLI for all state. `forge setup` copies it to
+`.opencode/plugins/forge-workflow/index.ts`. The artifact and its delivery path ship in the npm
+package: `plugin/opencode/` is added to `package.json files[]`, to `lib/package-root.js`
+`ASSET_ROOTS`, and to the embedded-assets drift test (review found both currently exclude
+`plugin/`, so setup could not read the artifact in npm installs or the compiled binary).
+
+Rejected alternatives:
+
+- **A. npm package `@forge/opencode-plugin` installed via `opencode plugin add`** — good for
+  global/zero-touch users, but adds a second publish channel, auto-install/cache failure modes
+  (`~/.cache/opencode/npm`), and version-skew against the beta. Kept as a **P4 opt-in**, not the
+  primary path.
+- **B. Plugin that imports `@opencode/plugin` for types/helpers** — verified hazard: the registry
+  `latest` is a placeholder (`0.0.0-reserved`), only `beta` has code, the CLI injects no runtime
+  deps, and users must install matching deps next to the plugin. Plain default export + raw JSON
+  Schema inputs + `Bun.spawn` removes the entire dependency-resolution class of failures.
+- **C. No plugin; rely on `.agents/skills` discovery only** — zero enforcement surface; loses the
+  point of the feature. Retained as the fallback if P0 falsifiers fire.
+
+## Success criteria
+
+Phase-gated; each gate is a hard stop with a go/no-go falsifier.
+
+- **P0 (contract lock, probe harness)**: every API assumption the design depends on is verified
+  against the pinned beta by a scripted probe (load/discovery, tool add/execute, command execute,
+  skill discovery precedence, event subscribe, `session.hook("context")`, `permission.hook("evaluate")`
+  firing + failure semantics, storage, Windows `forge` spawn, packaging delivery). Probe runs
+  locally, not in CI; `p0-findings.md` records evidence per check, captures the exact
+  `GET /api/plugin` envelopes for one active and one failed plugin (or substitutes log-based
+  evidence), and records a go/no-go per phase. Falsifier: any P0 check red → cut the affected
+  phase, degrade to P1-minimal, or stop.
+- **P1 (read-only orientation)**: `forge setup` on an opencode2 machine writes the vendored plugin
+  and it reaches `state.status=active` (envelope captured in P0); pointer-only orientation (issue
+  id, stage, artifact paths) injected on session context; read-only commands `/forge-status` and
+  `/forge-ready` execute and render CLI JSON; kill switch `rail.opencode_plugin` (registered in
+  `runtime-graph.js`, default-on, unlocked) disables everything; all fail-open. Unit tests cover
+  the artifact surface, install helper, registry changes; packaging includes the artifact; repo
+  drift tests updated.
+- **P2 (tools + permission bridge)**: read-only Forge verbs as native tools with typed schemas
+  (raw JSON Schema, `output` schema declared); mutating verbs exist but require explicit option
+  opt-in. Permission bridge is **ask-only** (never deny), performs zero CLI/tool work inside
+  `evaluate`, has a timeout, fails open, and reads `forge control status --json` per event (no
+  cache). Kill switch honored.
+- **P3 (events + session hooks)**: event subscription persists **metadata-only**, retention-capped
+  notes to plugin storage (never committed, redacted, no prompt text); session context stays
+  pointer-only; no silent kernel writes — kernel mutation only through explicit user-invoked tools.
+- **P4 (TUI + dynamic/MCP, opt-in)**: TUI status slot and MCP transform gated on P0–P3 being
+  load-bearing through a release cycle; npm package for global install if P2 evidence warrants.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- opencode **1.x** (`@opencode-ai/plugin` hooks era) support. v1 users keep today's status quo
+  (`.agents/skills` + AGENTS.md); setup refuses politely on v1-only machines.
+- Re-introducing opencode **mirror directories** (`.opencode/skills`, command files) unless P0
+  proves `.agents/skills` is not discovered by v2.
+- Kernel schema changes, new CLI verbs, or moving issue state into plugin storage.
+- Auto-claim, auto-close, auto-push, auto-merge — no mutating action without an explicit user
+  invocation.
+- TUI work in P1–P3.
+
+## Constraints
+
+1. **Exact version pinning.** Plugin contract and probe target `0.0.0-beta-19425`. Supported
+   matrix: ≤2 consecutive opencode2 betas; `forge doctor` reports resolved vs tested version,
+   derived from the contract fixture (single source of truth).
+2. **Zero runtime imports in the plugin artifact.** Raw JSON Schema for tool inputs/outputs; the
+   only runtime APIs are opencode-provided globals (`Bun.spawn`) and the context object. Types
+   (dev-only) are allowed in generator tests, never in the artifact.
+3. **The kernel is the sole authority.** Plugin state (storage) is derived/operational only; all
+   issue-state reads/writes go through `forge` CLI JSON (`forge.issue.v1`, `forge.gate.v1`).
+   Rail state is read via `forge control status --json` (`{items:[{id,surface,state,locked}]}`,
+   no schema envelope — accepted deviation, documented).
+4. **Actor identity per spawn.** Every `forge` invocation from the plugin sets `FORGE_ACTOR=opencode`,
+   `FORGE_SESSION_ID=<opencode sessionID>`, `FORGE_WORKTREE_ID=<basename>` — without this, writes
+   are indistinguishable and can replay as duplicate-ok (`lib/forge-issues.js:148-190`).
+5. **Windows-safe process invocation.** Setup resolves an absolute runnable `forge` (prefer the
+   `.exe`/Bun shim; npm `.cmd` shims break `execFile` with `EINVAL` on Windows — verified), and
+   the artifact uses `Bun.spawn([absPath, ...argv])`, never a shell string.
+6. **Read-only default; mutations opt-in.** Orientation, read tools, and metadata notes default on.
+   Anything that writes to the kernel requires an explicit option and/or an explicit user command.
+7. **Fail-open.** Plugin load failure, CLI failure, timeout, or schema mismatch must degrade to
+   "no opinion" with one warning line — never block a session or a tool call.
+
+## Edge cases (decisions)
+
+| Case | Decision |
+|---|---|
+| Plugin not loaded / failed state | Session continues; P0 captures the failed `GET /api/plugin` envelope (or log line); `forge doctor` surfaces it with the log ref; setup prints one warning |
+| `forge` binary missing at runtime (GUI-launched server, PATH differences) | Fail-open; orientation skipped; commands return a one-line "forge unavailable" message |
+| Worktree / nested directory | `cwd` comes from the plugin location or session context; never assume repo root; identity env pinned per spawn |
+| opencode1.x only installed | Setup detects and refuses opencode plugin install with an explicit message; no v1-shaped files written |
+| Wrong-track package present (`.opencode/node_modules/@opencode-ai/plugin`) | Setup quarantines by rename to `@opencode-ai/plugin.quarantined-<ts>` (reversible; documented reverse path), warns, never builds against it |
+| Duplicate skill IDs (`.agents/skills` + registration + mirror) | Never register a skill that discovery already provides; P0 settles precedence with fake HOME; single source |
+| Gate state changed while session runs | Permission bridge re-reads `forge control status --json` per evaluate; no caching |
+| Beta bump breaks a hook shape | Contract probe fails → keep the last-supported pinned matrix; doctor reports mismatch; feature degrades, gates do not |
+| Plugin hot reload (transforms re-run) | All transforms idempotent (verified: transforms re-run repeatedly in v2) |
+| User edits the generated plugin | Setup overwrites generated output; `forge doctor` reports a drift hash; user edits belong in the authored source (`plugin/opencode/index.ts`), never the generated copy |
+| Session title / compaction hooks | Not touched in v1 (beta stream semantics); context hook only |
+| Server unreachable / auth required for readiness checks | Doctor falls back to log-based detection (no credentials on any command line; the probe's own server gets an ephemeral password via env) |
+
+## Ambiguity policy
+
+Use the 7-dimension rubric scoring per `/dev` decision gate. ≥80% confidence: proceed and
+document the decision in `decisions.md`. <80%: stop and ask. Phase gates (P0→P1→…) are hard
+human checkpoints regardless of confidence.
+
