+### Risk register (top)
+
+| Risk | Mitigation |
+|---|---|
+| Beta churn breaks plugin load silently | Exact pin; load-failure visibility capture in P0; doctor status; ≤2-version matrix; fail-open |
+| Wrong-track package (already on disk) | Detect/quarantine; doctor asserts registered+active; zero-dep artifact removes the import class |
+| Permission gate deadlock / double enforcement | Ask-only, no CLI calls in evaluate, no caching, fail-open; commit-time policy stays with lefthook |
+| Skill duplication/staleness | P0 settles discovery with fake HOME; single source; never register duplicate IDs |
+| Windows spawn ENOENT/EINVAL/injection | Absolute `.exe`/Bun shim resolved at setup; `Bun.spawn` argv arrays; widened metacharacter tests |
+| Artifact missing from npm/compiled installs | `files[]` + `ASSET_ROOTS` + embedded-assets drift + `npm pack --dry-run` assertion |
+| Load-failure state not visible in `GET /api/plugin` | P0 captures both envelopes; if failed-state absent, doctor falls back to log evidence |
+| Doctor readiness requires server auth | Log-based fallback; no credentials on command lines |
+| Secret/prompt leakage into notes | Metadata-only; redaction deny-list; retention cap; storage outside git; fixture test |
+| Maintenance rot / YAGNI | Kill switch; P2–P4 gated on evidence; TUI last; named version-bump owner |
+| Silent kernel writes | Read-only default; mutations only via explicit user-invoked verbs |
+
+### Version matrix and release contract
+
+- Tested: `@opencode/cli@0.0.0-beta-19425` + `@opencode/plugin@0.0.0-beta-19425`.
+- Support window: current and previous opencode2 beta (n=2). Outside window: plugin no-ops with a
+  doctor warning; gates never depend on the plugin.
+- **Owner/cadence**: Forge maintainers own the pin. Bump process: bump the pin in the contract
+  fixture → run the P0 probe → update `p0-findings.md` evidence + doctor window → release note.
+  Trigger: each opencode2 beta publish or monthly, whichever is first.
+- `forge setup` and `forge doctor` detect: opencode2 CLI present (version output contains
+  `opencode2` or resolves `@opencode/cli`); plugin dir present; artifact hash matches generated;
+  wrong-track dir present; rail state; optional server `GET /api/plugin` state (env-password
+  server or log fallback).
