+## Wave P2 — native tools + ask-only permission bridge (gated; decompose at gate)
+
+Outcome: native Forge tools for read verbs (`forge_ready`, `forge_show`, `forge_recap`,
+`forge_status`, `forge_recall`) with raw JSON Schema input/output; mutating verbs
+(`forge_claim`, `forge_comment`, `forge_close`, `forge_remember`) registered but inert unless
+`options.allowMutations: true`. Permission bridge: `permission.hook("evaluate")` sets `ask` or
+leaves the event untouched — never `deny`; state read from `forge control status --json` before
+the decision (zero subprocess/tool calls inside `evaluate`); timeout; fail-open.
+Acceptance: T7 evidence supports the hook semantics; bridge invariant tests green; probe still
+active. **Test strategy note**: the artifact is zero-import, so P2 tests are static source
+assertions + probe evidence (same pattern as T16/T21), not unit imports of the artifact.
+
+## Wave P3 — event notes + session hooks (gated)
+
+Outcome: `event.subscribe` records metadata-only notes (event type, timestamp, ids, hashes) to
+`ctx.storage` with a retention cap (bounded scan); redaction deny-list applied before
+persistence; never persists prompt text; `session.hook("context")` remains pointer-only; optional
+session `title` hook behind `options.sessionTitle: true`. No kernel writes.
+Acceptance: redaction fixture test; storage scan shows no prompt payloads; no title/compaction
+stream handling.
+
+## Wave P4 — TUI + MCP + npm channel (gated, opt-in)
+
+Outcome: `@opencode/plugin/tui` status slot showing current issue/stage; `ctx.mcp.transform`
+surfacing a Forge MCP server if/when one exists; publishable npm package for global install
+(`opencode plugin add`) with an explicit `files[]` decision.
+Acceptance: P0–P3 load-bearing for a release cycle; explicit demand evidence.
